{"id": "EUVD-2026-101129", "enisaUuid": "aed28483-3700-3060-8273-250ceb914706", "description": "miniupnpc through 2.3.3 contains a one-byte heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in the minixml parseelt function's namespace-prefix handling that skips an end-of-buffer check after advancing past ':'. A malicious or spoofed UPnP gateway on the local network can send a device description or SOAP reply ending in ':' within an element name to crash the client.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T15:01:23", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T15:01:23", "baseScore": 2.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:A/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/miniupnpc-minixml-oob-read", "https://github.com/miniupnp/miniupnp/blob/bf4215a7574f88aa55859db9db00e3ae58cf42d6/miniupnpc/src/minixml.c#L141", "https://github.com/miniupnp/miniupnp/commit/64ef08a12aabab57be0bf7e40f047c8f14dedf9c", "https://github.com/miniupnp/miniupnp", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/miniupnpc-through-2.3.3-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-minixml-parseelt"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110656", "GHSA-mpq5-p36j-xg57"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.29, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "d5b820b2-97b6-3e0a-8dbf-104ca52bef8f", "product": {"name": "miniupnpc", "vendor": {"name": "miniupnp project"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.3.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1d034b11-5e4f-3039-a640-404f053abfc1", "vendor": {"name": "miniupnp project"}}], "isExploited": false}